# @tandonmitul27 -- gem5 and DRAMsim3 are fetched and built by setup.sh,
# never committed: the built tree is ~5 GB, and vendoring upstream source
# would hide our changes (which live in patches/ and configs/ instead).
# no trailing slash: setup.sh makes a directory here, but a developer
# pointing at an existing build makes a SYMLINK, and "/gem5/" matches only
# the former -- the symlink would be committed.
/gem5

# run outputs
/out/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
m5out/
stats.txt

# Generated outputs: 'make sweep' rebuilds these in ~30 min. Committing them
# means a stale copy silently outlives any change to the model.
/results/*.parquet

# data/routing/ IS tracked, deliberately. The logs are input, not output:
# they cannot be rebuilt without the checkpoints (87 GiB for Mixtral) and a
# GPU, and nothing in analytical/ runs without them. 43 MB is the price of a
# repository that works on clone.
